-- ============================================================================
-- compliance PROFESSIONAL DEEP SEED: Compliance, Audit & Quality, intermediate
-- tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE PLAN, THE NONCONFORMANCE AND THE CHECKLIST. A hold
-- point stops work and a witness point does not; a decision is a date and a
-- named verifier, and a waiver carries its reason; progress is counted from
-- the points and from the answers, never typed; a plan, an NCR, an audit and a
-- programme each close only through a gate that names what is missing; an
-- auditor may not audit their own area; and an open NCR ages until it closes.
--
-- THE ENGINE FACT THIS TIER OWNS. A request is not a result. Removing a point,
-- waiving it or passing it goes through a gate first, and a refused request
-- changes nothing on the plan.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. "Not applicable" is an answer only with its
-- reason, a failed point is the most outstanding item on a plan, and a
-- cancelled audit is not a delivered one.
--
-- ONE RULE, NOW: an audit cancelled without a written reason is outstanding in
-- programmeProgress, canCompleteProgramme and summarise alike, and every
-- percent rounds half up on the exact fraction (ASC-0). The capstone grades
-- four engine percents and two NCR ages, at a tolerance of 0.5.
-- ============================================================================

values ('compliance', 'intermediate', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-the-inspection-and-test-plan","title":"The Inspection and Test Plan","lesson_keys":["l01-five-point-types-and-one-that-stops-work","l02-a-decision-is-a-date-and-a-name","l03-a-waiver-carries-its-reason","l04-setting-a-hold-point-aside","l05-progress-counted-from-the-points"]},{"key":"m02-closing-a-plan","title":"Closing a Plan","lesson_keys":["l01-a-failed-point-blocks-whatever-its-type","l02-hold-points-outstanding","l03-an-open-ncr-blocks-the-plan","l04-removing-a-point-and-raising-an-ncr"]},{"key":"m03-the-nonconformance","title":"The Nonconformance","lesson_keys":["l01-the-disposition-comes-first","l02-severity-sets-what-closure-needs","l03-a-completed-action-and-a-working-one","l04-ageing-and-its-four-bands","l05-what-the-dashboard-counts"]},{"key":"m04-the-checklist","title":"The Checklist","lesson_keys":["l01-not-applicable-needs-a-reason","l02-no-checklist-is-no-percentage","l03-a-failed-critical-item-needs-a-finding","l04-stop-work-records-its-correction"]},{"key":"m05-the-audit-and-the-programme","title":"The Audit and the Programme","lesson_keys":["l01-six-statuses-and-the-moves-between-them","l02-what-reporting-an-audit-needs","l03-what-closing-an-audit-needs","l04-the-lead-auditor-and-the-auditee","l05-a-programme-is-delivered-by-its-reports"]},{"key":"m06-the-professional-reading","title":"The Professional Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-abam-plan-end-to-end","l02-the-abam-audit-and-programme-end-to-end","l03-what-the-next-tier-changes"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
